
A short listing of lisp files - See Index.doc for explanations and notes.
   
ABC  Puts text entities in vertical alphabetical order.
ACH  Chgtext for attributes.
ALIGN  Converts text to aligned text.
AT  Quick attribute string changer.
ATTNAME  Changes an attribute to the drawing name, without path.
ATTX  Text changer - works on text and unblocked attributes.
AXE  Removes first or last word from text or add a new one.
BATCH  A simple batch and script file writer.
BEEP  Makes a beep.
BLAM  Explodes a block and replaces all of its attributes with text.
BLCHG  Inserts a new block at each insertion of an old one.
BLG  Resets the bulge factor in each segment of a polyline to a new value.
BLOCKED  Changes an attribute in every insertion of one block.
BOO   Zoom extents, draw a temporary box around the previous view.
BOOM   Zoom previous, draw a temporary box around the previous view.
BOX   A better than usual rectangle drawer.
BOXX   A debugging aid for LYNX. (see LYNX )
CENTRE   Converts text to centre justified text.
CHEC   Cyclic recursion checker.  Looks busy while you waste time.
CHG   Directly edit entity data listing.
CHGX   Directly edit entity data listing, allows subentity access.
CLEANER   Anytime complete drawing purge.
CLK   Draws a clock, set to the correct time.
CT   Multiple text lines, prefix, incremented letter, suffix.
CURL   Moves entities to the current layer.
DAB   Draws a line with breaks at intervals and blocks in them.
DEROT   Derotates blocks and text.
DIRT   Writes a names only dir listing to a file.  Alphabetic, no extensions.
DIRTX   Writes Dir to file, more options than Dirt.lsp.
EARTH   Draws a circle round the drawing the same size as the Earth.
ED   Edit text entities while in a drawing using your choice of editors.
EXPL   Explodes blocks with different X, Y and Z scale factors.
FIBL   Locates all inserts of a block in the drawing.
FIND   Find files from within a drawing.
FINDX  Find files, checks for other extensions.
FINTX   Finds text strings, mark entities containing them.
FIT   Converts text to fitted text.
GET   Prints the data for a selected entity to the screen.
HT   Text height changer.  Allows example selection.
HVB   Moves text insertion points vertically to lie on same horizontal line.
IHI   Inserts a circle on a line and trim out the centre.
IHI2   Inserts a block on a line and chop out the centre.
IHI3   Inserts a circle, trim out the centre, erase and insert a block.
INF   Prints (to the screen) various useful information about the drawing.
JACK   Inserts a block at a scale equal to Dimscale.
L   Error handler, sysvar initializer and lisp loader.
LAC   Composite line (10 units long) & circle (2 units diameter) maker.
LAC1   Converts existing lines to line & circle.  10 & 2, as Lac.lsp
LACC   Line & circle maker, input length, gap, diameter.
LADD   Combines two lines of text.
LC   Layer change with screen menu.
LCH   Moves objects to a new layer by selecting an entity thereon.
LCS   Changes text to lower case.
LD   Lisp loader.
LEFT   Converts text to left justified text.
LIC   Change a line, move the end closest to the pick point.
LIX   Sets the limits to the extents.
LSET   Pick an object and thus set the current layer.
LT   Changes linetype by example selection.
LTR   Write personal letters from within AutoCAD.
LYNX   Combines a number of lines into one.
MIDDLE   Converts text to middle justified text.
MVA   Moves the lower left point of the drawing to 0,0.
NAMB   Get just the name of a picked block.
NT   Incremented numbers with text.
NUM   Changes existing text to sequential numbers.
NUMTX   A variation of Num: allows a prefix and a suffix.
ONE  Prints the equivalent of a numeral in English.
OTX   Text at a chosen spacing and angle.  Defaults for everything.
PID   Adds a prefix or suffix (or both) to a text string.
PKILL   Locates and optionally removes all point entities from a drawing.
PL   Plot initiate utility.  Uses most recent defaults.  See Plonk.
PLANT   Automatic plant maker.
PLDT   Changes a selected attribute in a selected block to the date.
PLONK   Automatic plot file generator - stores plot info in drawing.
PNEUM   Pneumatic line constructor.
PROP   Sets the X, Y and Z scales in a number of blocks to 1.
PROPS   Like Prop, sets scales to existing X, Y, or Z or to another number.
QUONSET   Sets an attribute to the drawing name (without path).
RA   Redraw with timer.
RAN   Random number generator.
RIGHT   Converts text to right justified text.
RT   Reaction time tester.
RTALL   Reverses the order of letters in every text string in a drawing.
RTX   Reverses just one text string.
SC   Style change with screen menu.
SCR   Script loader.
SDEL   Get selection set, erase only entities of a specified type.
SHUX   Text vertical spacing adjuster.
SING   Break the first line of two selected.
SIX   Lottery ticket number generator (for the 649 format).
SL   Erases the second last entity created.
SLYNX   Same as Lynx.lsp but puts lines on snap and on the current layer.
SNAKE   Puts entities on snap, mashes to fit.
SNAME   Puts the drawing name in the upper right hand corner of the screen.
SNAPPER   Moves the insertion point of entities to the nearest snap point.
SPARE   Removes spaces from both ends of text strings.
SPRAY   Wraps text around entities.
SPYR   Automatic spiral pattern drawer.
SQ   Sequential text changer.
ST   Short style changer.  No screen menu.
STAR   Superimpose the drawing on a slide.
SWX   Switch positions of two groups of entities.
TACH   Sucks text out of a text entity and put it into an attribute.
TB   Terminal block drawer.
TBTX   Terminal block drawer with prefix and suffix and at angles.
TCH   Changes 1 or more text lines to a string, allows example selection.
TCHS  Single text changer.  One less keystroke than TCH.
TOGGLE   Toggles a system variable between 0 and 1.
TTC   Replace text: same string & height, current style & layer, centred.
TTF   Text to fit.
TTL   Text to left.
TTM   Text to middle.
TTR   Text to right.   See also Centre, Left, Right, Fit, Middle and Align.
TXD   Changes existing text to date - the long format: JULY 12, 1969.
TXMD   Text to metric date - DD/MM/YY format.
TXKILL   Finds empty text strings ("" or " ") and optionally eradicates them.
TXN   Text to title without path.
TXS   Global text size changer - you specify initial and desired sizes.
TXTT   Text to title with path.
TXX   Short, fast sequential text changer.
UC   Convertx text to upper case.
VB   Fit multiple text between two theoretical vertical lines.
VBC   Centre multiple text on a vertical line.
VBHX   Centre multiple text on a line if it's in the current text style.
VBL   Left justify multiple text on a vertical line.
VBM   Middle justify multiple text on a vertical line.
VBR   Right justify multiple text on a vertical line.
VVB   Respace a column of text vertically.
WMX   Move a word to the next line, or the previous one, or to a new line.
WT   Multiple width scale factor change.
XING   Multiple crossing locator and breaker.
XX   Shells out to a text editor with the file last loaded with Ld.lsp.
ZA   Zoom All with timer.
ZE   Zoom Extents without a regen.
ZP   Zoom Previous with timer.
ZVS   Zoom to the virtual screen limits with no regen.